OL,3,GNEWSAHistorical pub to become charity
OL,4,Ahub and offices
OL,5,
OL,6,FA historical pub that was knocked down
OL,7,Fand rebuilt because of the widening of
OL,8,Fthe A63 in Hull, will no longer be used
OL,9,Fas a hospitality venue.
OL,11,FDevelopers of the Castle Buildings
OL,12,Fregeneration project told a council
OL,13,Fplanning committee meeting that,
OL,14,Fdespite a considerable rebuild of the
OL,15,FEarl de Grey, there had been "no
OL,16,Finterest whatsoever" in reopening it as
OL,17,Fa pub, cafe or restaurant.
OL,19,FInstead, the building will be used as
OL,20,Foffices and a community hub by the
OL,21,Fcharity HEY Smile Foundation,
OL,22,Fdevelopers Wykeland Group said.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
